{"seq":1,"mint":"C17","verb":"claim","status":"ok","model":"openai/gpt-5.6-luna","approach":"split","literals":false,"findings":[{"kind":"contradicts","clause":"which is how `look --lines` already annotates a range only when it was clamped","clause_quoted":true,"facts":["F9","F16","F28","F32"],"quoted_from":"output","evidence":"    let (shown, label) = match lines {\n        None => (contents.clone(), path.to_string()),\n        Some((a, b)) => {\n            if a < 1 || a > b {\n                return Err(workspace::refuse(workspace_dir, \"look\", format!(\"invalid --lines range {a}:{b}\")));\n            }\n            let all: Vec<&str> = contents.lines().collect();\n            let total = all.len();\n            if a > total {\n                (String::new(), format!(\"{path} lines {a}-{b} (file has {total} line(s); nothing in range)\"))\n            } else {\n                let end = b.min(total);\n                (all[a - 1..end].join(\"\\n\"), format!(\"{path} lines {a}-{end}\"))\n            }\n        }\n    };","why":"The `Some((a, b))` branch formats a range label in both the clamped case and the ordinary in-file case; the `else` branch applies whenever `a <= total`, not only when `b` exceeds the file length.","quoted":true}],"at":1790113158,"cost":0.0076372,"elapsed_ms":43115,"attempts":2,"not_verbatim":0,"literals_refuted":0,"not_a_quantity":0,"kind_off_verb":0,"refuted":0}
